abstract: >-
  The carbon cost of seismic resilience: gravity-only versus seismic-aware
  form-finding of reinforced concrete shells. Shells are form-found with the
  force density method, with lateral seismic load following Michiels and
  Adriaenssens, sized in CalculiX against linear buckling, compression and
  deflection checks, and their A1-A3 embodied carbon counted. A pre-registered
  design space of 168 sized designs (84 paired comparisons) tests whether
  seismic-aware form-finding saves 5 % or more carbon against a gravity-only
  form sized for the same seismic level. Includes the frozen results record,
  verification checks, paper figures and an offline interactive explorer.
  Built on ShellBench's validated modules.
